# Backend Development Patterns

## FastAPI & API Development
- Use dependency injection: `db: Session = Depends(get_db)`
- Proper HTTP status codes, Pydantic models for validation
- Always use `get_effective_user` for authentication
- Validate user ownership for all resources

## SQLAlchemy & Database
- Inherit from [Base](mdc:backend/src/models/base.py)
- UUID primary keys, foreign keys with CASCADE deletes
- Add timestamps, index frequently queried fields
- Use service layer for all DB operations, `joinedload` for eager loading

## Service Layer
- Place logic in [services/](mdc:backend/src/services/)
- Stateless pure functions with dependency injection
- Return typed objects, not raw queries

## File Handling & AI Integration
- Use [file_service.py](mdc:backend/src/services/file_service.py)
- Validate file types and sizes before processing
- Use [ai_service.py](mdc:backend/src/services/ai_service.py)
- Handle API rate limits and errors, log AI usage

## Error Handling & Validation
- Use FastAPI's `HTTPException` for API errors
- Pydantic models for validation, custom validators in [utils/validation.py](mdc:backend/src/utils/validation.py)
- Sanitize inputs to prevent injection

## Background Tasks
- Use ThreadPoolExecutor for CPU-intensive tasks
- Manage database sessions properly, use asyncio for I/O-bound
- Always close sessions in finally blocks

## Code Quality
- PEP 8 with Black (90 chars), type hints for all parameters
- Comprehensive docstrings, meaningful names
- Import organization: stdlib, third-party, local
- Module docstrings for all files
- Pre-commit hooks enforce formatting and linting
